  "wiki": {
    "family": "Primulaceae",
    "nativeRegion": "Eastern Mediterranean (Turkey, Levant, Greek islands, North Africa)",
    "summary": "Cyclamen persicum is a tuberous perennial grown worldwide as a winter-flowering houseplant. Its heart-shaped, silver-marbled leaves rise from a flattened tuber, and swept-back flowers in pink, red, purple or white nod on slender stalks above the foliage. It goes dormant in summer in its native dry climate.",
